            <div xml:id="d932">

                <pb facs="0872" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/105</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-25T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25, 1918,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>733. Please report whether following statement alleged to have been made by
                        Mannerheim is authentic: <pb
                        facs="0873" n="783" xml:id="pg783"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Germans’ victorious and mighty army landed in Finland to help against
                            the infamous Bolsheviks, and to help the friendship the Finnish people
                            have always had for the noble Kaiser and mighty German people. Fighting
                            shoulder to shoulder with the great merman army the Finnish army should
                            be imbued with the discipline that has brought that army from victory to
                            victory. I greet the brave German troops and hope that every Finn will
                            realize the great sacrifice of the noble German people who are helping
                            them in an hour when every man is needed on the western
                        front.</p></quote></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
